Simplified Requirements for TMS (MVP v1.0)
Objective: To build a lightweight, fast, and straightforward Test Management System. It covers the fundamental QA lifecycle: "Write tests -> Group -> Execute -> Show results," while ensuring data integrity and professional reporting.
Module 1: Workspace, Project Management & Access Control
Authentication: The system uses predefined accounts instead of open registration. Access is restricted to admin (Admin role) and tester (Tester role) with hardcoded credentials.
Data Isolation: The system supports multiple projects. Each project acts as an isolated container. Every database query is automatically restricted to its specific Project ID to ensure no cross-project data leakage.
Role-Based Access Control (RBAC): * Admin: Full CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) permissions for projects, suites, test cases, and test runs.
Tester: Restricted access. Read-only for the repository; execute-only for test runs (change step statuses, attach evidence, add bug links).
Module 2: Test Repository (Management)
Grouping (Suites): Test cases are organized into single-level folders (Suites). No nested folder trees are allowed to maintain simplicity.
Deep Search: A global search bar allows users to instantly filter test cases by searching for keywords across Titles, Descriptions, Pre-conditions, Step Actions, and Expected Results.
Test Case Structure:
Header (Metadata): Title, Description, Pre-conditions, and Priority level (High, Medium, Low).
Steps (Array): A list of sequential, distinct objects. Each step contains two mandatory fields: "Action" and "Expected Result".
Attachments (EdgeMessage): Users can upload files (images, JSON/XML, logs) to a Test Case or Step. The system integrates with EdgeMessage API for storage and retrieval.
Import & Export:
Export: Users can export selected cases or suites into CSV or XML formats.
Import: Admins can bulk-import test cases via CSV or XML, automatically generating cases and their nested steps.
Module 3: Test Execution (Test Runs)
Run Creation: Users create a Test Run by providing a Title, Environment (e.g., "Staging"), and selecting suites or individual cases. The system creates a snapshot of the cases to preserve their state at the time of execution.
Granular Execution:
Testers execute runs step-by-step. Each individual step can be marked as Passed, Failed, or Skipped.
Atomic Failure: If any single step is marked as Failed, the entire Test Case automatically inherits the Failed status.
Failure Artifacts:
Evidence (screenshots, logs) can be attached directly to a specific step via EdgeMessage.
A "Bug URL" field allows testers to link a failed case to an external tracker (e.g., Jira).
Locking & Unlocking: * Lock: Marking a run as "Completed" locks it into a read-only state for historical integrity.
Unlock: Admins can "Unlock" a completed run to allow corrections or status updates.
Module 4: Reporting & Metrics
Real-time Statistics: Inside each Test Run, the system tracks:
Total (Count of all cases)
Passed / Failed / Untested (Both in absolute numbers and percentages).
Report Export: Users can download results as a PDF or CSV file. The report includes execution metrics, failed case details, and their associated Bug URLs.
